{
  "id": "typescript-14-module-resolution-modes",
  "slug": "module-resolution-modes",
  "title": "Module resolution: node, bundler, and nodenext",
  "moduleId": "typescript-14-modules-and-declarations",
  "order": 1,
  "hook": "`moduleResolution` controls import resolution — `nodenext` enforces Node ESM rules and package.json `exports`; `bundler` (TS 5+) matches Vite/esbuild. Wrong mode causes CI failures while IDE works.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "**node10** ignores exports. **node16/nodenext** enforce extensions, import/require rules, and `package.json` `\"type\"`. **bundler** allows extensionless imports for webpack/Vite. Pair **`module: nodenext`** with nodenext for Node libraries; **`module: ESNext` + bundler** for frontend apps."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "nodenext",
              "longForm": "Node ESM resolution",
              "plainDefinition": "Respects exports and .js extensions.",
              "example": "\"moduleResolution\": \"nodenext\""
            },
            {
              "term": "bundler",
              "longForm": "bundler resolution",
              "plainDefinition": "TS 5+ for tools that rewrite imports.",
              "example": "\"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\""
            },
            {
              "term": "exports",
              "longForm": "package.json exports",
              "plainDefinition": "Conditional subpath map.",
              "example": "\"exports\": { \".\": \"./dist/index.js\" }"
            },
            {
              "term": "ESM",
              "longForm": "ECMAScript modules",
              "plainDefinition": "import/export — .mjs or type module.",
              "example": "import \"./file.js\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "npm publish with wrong resolution breaks consumers. Monorepos mixing CJS/ESM need nodenext. bundler in libraries hides Node failures."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: extensionless in Node",
          "body": "nodenext requires `import \"./file.js\"` even when source is file.ts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Pick runtime",
              "body": "Node lib → nodenext; Vite → bundler"
            },
            {
              "title": "Align module",
              "body": "module + resolution match"
            },
            {
              "title": "Check type field",
              "body": "module vs commonjs"
            },
            {
              "title": "Verify exports",
              "body": "Subpaths in exports map"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Resolution modes",
            "source": "flowchart TD\n  IMP --> MODE{resolution}\n  MODE -->|nodenext| NODE[exports+extensions]\n  MODE -->|bundler| BUN[bundler rewrite]"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "nodenext .js import",
            "code": "import { helper } from \"./utils.js\"; // utils.ts source\n// import \"./utils\" // error under nodenext",
            "explanation": ".js extension for relative ESM."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "package exports",
            "code": "{\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": { \".\": { \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\", \"import\": \"./dist/index.js\" } }\n}",
            "explanation": "types + import conditions."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "Vite tsconfig",
            "code": "{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}",
            "explanation": "bundler for Vite apps."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: node10 ignores exports",
            "code": "import { x } from \"lib/internal\"; // nodenext errors if not in exports",
            "explanation": "Legacy resolution bypasses exports guard."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
